.TH ISHTARIA-SERVER 1 "2026" "ishtaria-server" "Ishtaria"
.SH NAME
ishtaria-server \- authoritative world server of the Ishtaria virtual planet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ishtaria-server
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICONFIG\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs one Ishtaria world: its simulation, PostgreSQL persistence and the
federation endpoint that links worlds through portals. The server is
authoritative for all game state; clients send intentions and render the
acknowledged results.
.PP
On start-up the server applies the versioned SQL migrations embedded in the
executable, then verifies or creates the world row named by
.BR server_name .
If \fB\-\-import\fR is given, a heightmap is imported first (see below); an
identical import is a no-op, a conflicting map, seed or ruleset is rejected.
.PP
The server listens on the address from
.BR listen
in the configuration (default \fB0.0.0.0:7400\fR) and serves the HTTP API used
by the \fBishtaria-client\fR game client and by federated peer worlds. It
shuts down gracefully on SIGTERM or when \fBishtaria-admin\fR schedules a
shutdown; in both cases connected clients receive a system message with the
remaining time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI [ CONFIG ]
Configuration file in TOML format.
Default: \fB/etc/ishtaria/server.toml\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-import " " \fIPGM\fR
Import a worldgen heightmap (binary P5 PGM strip of six square faces, up to
1024 pixels per face and 16 MiB) into the database. Requires \fB\-\-seed\fR.
The original file and decoded pixels are stored with a SHA-256 checksum;
PGM carries no seed, so the server cannot verify it matches the generator
input.
.TP
.BR \-\-seed " " \fISEED\fR
Seed of the imported heightmap. Required by \fB\-\-import\fR; the seed becomes
part of the world's deterministic identity.
.TP
.BR \-\-import\-only
Import the heightmap and exit without serving. Requires \fB\-\-import\fR.
Used by \fBishtaria-server-init\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-datadisks
Print the installed story datadisks (id, version, name) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-datadisks " " \fIIDS\fR
Check that the given comma-separated datadisk ids can be combined in one
world, and exit. Prints the number of datadisks, places and characters.
.TP
.BR \-\-print\-world\-terrain " " \fIIDS\fR
Print the equirectangular world terrain of the given comma-separated datadisk
ids (heightmap and water mask paths, TAB separated) for
\fBishtaria-worldgen \-\-earth\fR, and exit. Fails when none or several of the
datadisks define the planet.
.TP
.BR \-\-datadisk " " \fIID\fR
Story datadisk to apply to a world generated by this import. Repeatable.
Requires \fB\-\-import\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-solar\-offset\-seconds " " \fISECONDS\fR
Shift the world's solar clock by this many seconds at start-up (added to the
persisted offset). Range: \fB\-86400\fR to \fB86400\fR (±24 hours).
Default: \fB0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the server version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The TOML configuration file recognises these keys:
.TP
.B server_name
DNS name of this world; becomes part of every player and item id. Permanent
after the first import \(em choose carefully.
.TP
.B ruleset
Ruleset identifier shared with federated worlds (must match peers' major
version), for example \fBcore-rules@1.0\fR.
.TP
.B listen
Socket address to listen on. Default: \fB0.0.0.0:7400\fR.
.TP
.B database_url
PostgreSQL connection string. Overridden by the \fBDATABASE_URL\fR
environment variable.
.TP
.B public_url
HTTPS address other worlds and players use to reach this server; enables
federation. Omit for a private server.
.TP
.B atmosphere
Optional atmosphere description announced to clients.
.TP
.B [federation]
Optional federation policy: \fBpolicy\fR (\fBclosed\fR, \fBapprove\fR or
\fBopen\fR) and \fBallow_private_peers\fR (development networks only).
.TP
.B [limits]
Optional public-server protection: per-address token-bucket rate limits
(\fBauth_per_minute\fR, \fBrequests_per_second\fR, \fBburst\fR),
\fBtrust_proxy\fR, \fBaccess_log\fR and \fBmetrics_token\fR. The defaults suit
a public server.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DATABASE_URL
PostgreSQL connection string. Overrides \fBdatabase_url\fR in the
configuration. Required when the configuration does not set it.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_DATADISK_DIR
Directory with installed story datadisks.
Default: \fB/usr/share/ishtaria/datadisks\fR.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_ASSETS_DIR
Directory with the files the server itself ships (music, knowledge cards).
Default: \fB/usr/share/ishtaria-server\fR.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_SETTLEMENTS
Number of generated settlements per world (0 for none, at most 200).
Default: \fB36\fR.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_PAYMENT_SECRET
Secret for the optional monetization endpoint. At least 16 characters;
never commit it.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_CONFIG
Default configuration path used by \fBishtaria-server-init\fR.
Default: \fB/etc/ishtaria/server.toml\fR.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_TEST_HEIGHTMAP
Test-only path to a heightmap for the PostgreSQL integration tests.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_TEST_CLIENT
Test-only flag enabling additional client tests against a test server.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_SLIDE_CAPTURE
Test-only path for a captured movement trajectory replayed by client tests.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/ishtaria/server.toml
Configuration file (mode 0640, group \fBishtaria\fR).
.TP
.B /usr/share/ishtaria/datadisks/
Installed story datadisks.
.TP
.B /usr/share/ishtaria-server/
Server assets: music and knowledge-card images.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ishtaria-server
Start the server with the default configuration
(\fB/etc/ishtaria/server.toml\fR).
.TP
.B ishtaria-server /etc/ishtaria/server.toml \-\-import planet.pgm \-\-seed 42 \-\-import\-only
Import a heightmap as seed 42 and exit without serving.
.TP
.B ishtaria-server \-\-list\-datadisks
List the installed story datadisks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ishtaria-admin (1),
.BR ishtaria-client (1)
.PP
.BR ishtaria-server-init (8)
generates a planet with \fBishtaria-worldgen\fR and imports it once.
.BR ishtaria-worldgen (1)
generates the deterministic heightmap strip the server imports.
